# TMX Assistant — AI chat panel for tournament directors
# Set to the assistant service URL. Leave empty to disable.
# Local dev: http://localhost:3200
# Production (nest): https://assistant.courthive.net
VITE_ASSISTANT_URL=

# Score-relay — Phase 4 crowd promotion UI.
# Used to call score-relay's /api/crowd-sessions/* endpoints from the
# matchUp three-dot menu ("View crowd trackers (N)"). Crowd data never
# transits competition-factory-server (Decision 6).
# Local dev: http://localhost:8384
# Production: https://courthive.net (or wherever score-relay is fronted)
VITE_SCORE_RELAY_URL=

# Service worker — offline app shell. OFF unless set to `true` or `1`.
#
# A service worker outlives the deployment that installed it: a bad one pins
# users to a stale build and cannot be fixed by shipping new files, because the
# stale worker decides whether they are fetched. So this is a kill-switch, not
# just an on-switch — unsetting it and redeploying REMOVES the worker from every
# client that loads the app (see src/serviceWorker.ts).
#
# Updates never apply under the operator: a new build waits and surfaces the
# existing "update ready" notice rather than swapping the engine out mid-match.
VITE_SERVICE_WORKER=
